 "How do motorized curtains differ from hand-drawn curtains?",
 "A motor opens and closes them instead of pulling the fabric by hand — ideal for wide or tall windows, or rooms where everyday convenience matters. The fabric feel and light control still depend on the curtain style and fabric you choose.",
 "How do I choose fabric so the motor runs smoothly?",
 "Fabric that is too heavy or an unbalanced rail adds load to the motor. After on-site measuring, our team matches fabric type, width and motor model so you get the light control you want without straining the system.",
 "How do I care for the system and fabric?",
 "Dust the rail and the outside of the motor regularly, and don't force the fabric when the system jams. Care for the fabric according to its material, as with ordinary curtains. If anything seems wrong, stop using it and book an inspection.",
 "What power and space do I need to prepare for installation?",
 "You need a power point or a wiring plan for the motor model, and the space above the window frame must be able to take the motor rail. Some rooms can use rechargeable or battery motors — our technician will recommend the right approach for your building after surveying the site.",
 "Can it connect to a smart home, and what is warranted?",
 "Many models support remote, app or smart home gateways depending on the model spec; compatibility depends on your home system. Installation is warranted under standard terms, and the motor under the manufacturer's terms stated in the quote.",
