 "How do roller blinds differ from curtains?",
 "Roller blinds roll up above the frame, saving side space and giving clean lines, while curtains offer more fabric depth and warmth. Roller blinds are often chosen for offices, condos and large glass windows.",
 "What is the difference between sunscreen and blackout?",
 "Sunscreen filters light and keeps some of the view; blackout reduces light more and gives more privacy. How much heat is reduced depends on fabric type, sun direction and the building's existing glass.",
 "How do I clean roller blinds?",
 "Dust regularly with a dry or microfibre cloth. Avoid soaking the whole panel unless the fabric supports it. Wipe spots gently following the instructions for the fabric type.",
 "Are there limits on size and roller box depth?",
 "Very wide windows may need to be split into sets. The roll depth when fully raised must not hit the ceiling or cornice. Our technician checks the frame, handles and window opening angle on site.",
 "What do price and installation time depend on?",
 "Window size, fabric type, chain/spring and number of sets determine the price. Stock fabrics are faster than special-order fabrics. Installation is warranted under standard terms after handover.",
