 "How is a Magic Screen blind different from a regular roller blind?",
 "The fabric alternates sheer and opaque bands; sliding it lines the bands up to let light through or block it finely. A regular roller blind controls light across the whole panel according to a single fabric type. It's a middle ground between enjoying the view and keeping privacy.",
 "How fine is the light control, and does it black out fully?",
 "Adjusting the bands cuts glare well, but it's generally not as dark as a full blackout fabric. For a very dark bedroom, pair it with blackout curtains or choose a denser fabric as advised on site.",
 "How do I clean it without misaligning the bands?",
 "Dust gently along the bands and avoid hard scrubbing that can shift the fabric layers. Don't soak the whole panel unless necessary. For stubborn stains, book an assessment for the right care method.",
 "Are there width limits for installation?",
 "Very wide windows may be split into several sets so the bands stay straight and roll smoothly. Cassette spacing and levelling must be precise — have our installers measure and install for neatly parallel bands.",
 "Size, band fabric type, colour and chain or motor system affect the price. Special-order colours take longer than standard stock. Lead time is confirmed after on-site measuring and material confirmation.",
