 "How are aluminium blinds different from wooden blinds?",
 "Aluminium is lighter, more moisture-resistant and easier to clean — ideal for offices and rooms that need frequent care. Wood emphasises natural tones and luxury. Choose by your room's style and humidity.",
 "How well do they control light and reduce heat?",
 "Tilting the slats cuts glare and reflections well. Heat reduction depends on slat colour, sun direction and the existing glass. For more opacity, close the slats to overlap and check edge light gaps after installation.",
 "How do I clean them without bending the slats?",
 "Wipe one slat at a time with a soft cloth or a microfibre clip-on duster. Avoid bending slats hard or pouring water on the cord mechanism. Wipe kitchen grease off right away with a mild cleaner.",
 "Can they be fitted to very tall or wide windows?",
 "Yes, but slat weight and length must be calculated. Some jobs are split into sets or use a suitable slat width. Our installers measure on site to check the frame, handles and window opening clearance.",
 "Size, number of sets, slat colour and tilt system determine the price. Stock colours are faster than made-to-order colours. Installation is warranted under our standard terms.",
