 "How are vertical blinds different from roller blinds?",
 "Vertical blinds use vertical vanes that tilt and slide open — ideal for tall or long windows. Roller blinds are a single panel that rolls up and down with cleaner lines. Office buildings favour vertical blinds for their good control of screen glare.",
 "How do I choose vanes to control light and reduce glare?",
 "Opaque vanes block sun and add privacy; more sheer vanes give soft light. Light colours reflect light differently from dark ones. Our team recommends tones and vane types based on sun direction and desk layout.",
 "Can they be maintained and the vanes replaced?",
 "Dust periodically with microfibre. In many systems, damaged vanes can be replaced individually. Avoid twisting the vanes beyond their designed angle.",
 "Are there limits for curved windows or sliding doors?",
 "Long, straight windows are best. Corners, curves or sliding doors need a specially designed track and vane stacking point — have our installers measure on site and test the door opening clearance before production.",
