 "How does a solid partition differ from one with acrylic windows?",
 "A solid partition divides space and blocks sight and airflow more clearly. Euro/USA partitions with acrylic windows are more see-through and let in more light. Choose solid when you need privacy or want to zone the air-con.",
 "Does it really keep air-con in and reduce noise?",
 "A solid partition reduces airflow between zones so the air-con works more efficiently in the area you use. It only partly reduces noise — not as much as a permanent built wall.",
 "Wipe with a soft cloth and mild cleaner. Avoid sharp objects and strong solvents that damage the PVC surface. Keep the bottom track free of dust and anything that blocks sliding.",
 "What space and structure does installation need?",
 "We measure width, height and floor-to-ceiling levels so the partition folds all the way. Some sites need an extra beam or levelling. Our technician surveys the site before producing the actual height.",
 "What do price and installation time depend on?",
 "Opening size, number of panels, colour/pattern and site difficulty are the main factors. Urgent jobs depend on the production queue. Installation is warrantied under the terms in the quote.",
