 "How are plastic strip curtains different from roller shutters or partitions?",
 "Overlapping PVC strips let people and vehicles pass frequently while still blocking dust and insects and holding temperature — unlike roller shutters, which open and close occasionally, and partitions, which are mainly for dividing rooms",
 "How do I choose strip thickness and type?",
 "Cold rooms, large kitchens and loading halls use different thicknesses and strip formulas. Clear strips keep traffic visible; anti-insect or anti-fog formulas are available depending on use — our team recommends after a site survey",
 "How do I clean and replace strips?",
 "Wipe periodically with a cleaner suitable for plastic. Cloudy, torn or hardened strips can be replaced individually without removing the whole set, minimising downtime",
 "What needs to be measured for a doorway installation?",
 "Width, height, door opening direction and forklift clearance. Strip overlap must be enough to block drafts without obstructing traffic. Our technicians survey industrial sites before installation",
 "What do price and service life depend on?",
 "Door size, number of strips, thickness and material formula determine the price. Service life depends on traffic frequency, sunlight and chemicals in the area — lifespan is not guaranteed to be the same in every factory",
